.TH XNVME-PERF-RUN 1 "13 October 2026" "xNVMe" "xNVMe"
.SH NAME
\fBxnvme-perf-run \fP- Run a time-bounded async IO benchmark against one or more NVMe devices.
\fBDevices are distributed across CPU threads pinned by \fB--cpumask\fP or \fB--cpulist\fP.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.fam C
\fBxnvme-perf\fP \fIrun\fP [<uri>\.\.\.] [<args>]
.fam T
.fi
.fam T
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a time-bounded async IO benchmark against one or more NVMe devices.
Devices are distributed across CPU threads pinned by \fB--cpumask\fP or \fB--cpulist\fP.
.SH REQUIRED
.TP
.B
\fB--iopattern\fP STRING
IO pattern (read, write, randread, randwrite)
.TP
.B
\fB--qdepth\fP NUM
Use given 'NUM' as queue max capacity
.TP
.B
\fB--iosize\fP NUM
Use given 'NUM' as bs/iosize
.TP
.B
\fB--runtime\fP NUM
Run for 'NUM' seconds
.RE
.PP

.SH OPTIONAL
.TP
.B
[uri \.\.\.]
Device URI e.g. '/dev/nvme0n1', '0000:01:00.1', '10.9.8.1:8888', '\\.\PhysicalDrive1'
.TP
.B
[ \fB--nqueues\fP NUM ]
Number of queues per device
.TP
.B
[ \fB--cpumask\fP STRING ]
Hex CPU bitmask for thread pinning (e.g. 0x3)
.TP
.B
[ \fB--cpulist\fP STRING ]
Comma-separated list of CPU ids or CPU id ranges for thread pinning (e.g. 0-3,4,6)
.TP
.B
[ \fB--be\fP STRING ]
xNVMe backend, e.g. 'spdk', 'libvfn', 'upcie'
.TP
.B
[ \fB--subnqn\fP STRING ]
Subsystem NQN of the NVMe over Fabrics endpoint e.g. 'nqn.2022-06.io.xnvme:ctrlnode1'
.TP
.B
[ \fB--direct\fP ]
Bypass layers
.TP
.B
[ \fB--poll_io\fP NUM ]
For async={io_uring,libaio,kqueue}, enable hipri/io-compl.polling
.TP
.B
[ \fB--poll_sq\fP NUM ]
For async=io_uring, enable kernel-side sqthread-poll
.TP
.B
[ \fB--gpu_id\fP NUM ]
For be=upcie-cuda/upcie-hip, GPU ordinal to use
.TP
.B
[ \fB--homi-id\fP NUM ]
The HOMI identifier to share controllers under
.TP
.B
[ \fB--report-freq\fP FLOAT ]
Report progress every 'FLOAT' seconds
.TP
.B
[ \fB--help\fP ]
Show usage / help
.RE
.PP


